   "title": "read me",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## crop, edit, put back, compare\n\n**You need:** nothing (the sample facade stands in; or put a Load Image in its place). No models.\n\n**Do:** Queue once, so the crop node shows the picture. Then on *kubakub crop*: drag a box on the picture, drag\ninside it to move it, drag the handles to size it (Shift keeps the shape, Alt from the centre), double click = all\nof it. Pick a shape on the ratio pills (*original*, 1:1, 16:9 ...) and the size that comes out. Drag past the\npicture's edge to add canvas: the *new area* pills say how it is filled, and the `new_area` output is the mask for\nan outpaint. Queue again.\n\n**The edit in the middle** is a stand-in (it inverts the colours): put your sampler, upscaler or any edit there.\n*kubakub uncrop* puts the edited crop back where it came from, with a soft edge.\n\n**Compare:** swipe, side by side, difference, blink, onion; the corner button opens a big window with zoom.\nIt takes pictures and videos (a Load Video on `a` or `b`) and keeps both on the same frame.\n"
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## crop, edit, put back, compare\n\n**You need:** nothing (the sample facade stands in; or put a Load Image in its place). No models.\n\n**Do:** Queue once, so the crop node shows the picture. Then on *kubakub crop*: drag a box on the picture, drag\ninside it to move it, drag the handles to size it (Shift keeps the shape, Alt from the centre), double click = all\nof it. Pick a shape on the ratio pills (*original*, 1:1, 16:9 ...) and the size that comes out. Drag past the\npicture's edge to add canvas: the *new area* pills say how it is filled, and the `new_area` output is the mask for\nan outpaint. Queue again.\n\n**The edit in the middle** is a stand-in (it inverts the colours): put your sampler, upscaler or any edit there.\n*kubakub uncrop* puts the edited crop back where it came from, with a soft edge.\n\n**Compare:** swipe, side by side, difference, blink, onion; the corner button opens a big window with zoom.\nIt takes pictures and videos (a Load Video on `a` or `b`) and keeps both on the same frame.\n"
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
